to cover all this...)
Since there has already been talk about eating, I'd like to add my 2c worth...

The thing is, if you are interrupted while eating, how should the food be
handled ?  My suggestion is:
	if turns_used_eating <= 5
		food does not change, satiation level does not change
	else if turns_used_eating >= total_turns_to_eat_that_food_stuff - 5
		food is all eaten, satiation set accordingly
	else
		food becomes "leftovers", satiation set to 1/2 normal
This would make the food type "leftovers" necessary.  What about having
other human-type characters drop "leftovers" from time to time (this would
be a nice hint that there are such on this level).  Nonhumans would of
course like goblin' their food up till the last bite even though it's bad
for your 'elf :-)

Also, I think that quaffing and reading should also be possible without
picking the object in question up, as eating is.  Thus (standing on a it):
"There is a scroll called enchant armor hear, read it [ynq]" or
"There is a pink potion here, drink it [ynq]"
This way you would not have to mess around with dropping things to be able
to use things... of course, special cases would be in a shop, where the
object in question would be added to the "Used-up but not payed" list.
Zapping a wand should NOT be possible without picking it up, since you
obviously have to point the wand at it's intended target...
